  "body": "## What was wrong\n\nTelegram/Discord platforms started with **no allowlist** accepted any user/channel as operator — silently. No warning, no dashboard signal; the risk was invisible unless you already knew to check `.env`.\n\n## The fix (loud warning only — zero behavior change, per owner decision)\n\n- Startup warning per platform when running allowlist-free, naming the real env locks (`ALLOWED_TELEGRAM_USER_ID` / `ALLOWED_DISCORD_CHANNELS`).\n- New top-level config-payload field **`messaging_auth_open\": [...]`** (platform ids running open; `[]` when locked) so the dashboard can render the state.\n- Blank-after-strip counts as unconfigured everywhere; Discord's predicate delegates to the inbound parser so degenerate lists (`\",\"`) report open exactly as runtime treats them.\n\n## Verification\n\n24 new/green factory+payload tests; collateral suites green (94 admin, 54 startup-path); §66 mutations ×4 caught by name with byte-equal restores; ruff/format/ty clean. MINOR slot **5.52.0** (new admin-visible capability).\n\n## Residual risks\n\nPayload derives open-state from effective config rather than live runtime objects — identical semantics to what the startup warning inspects; documented in predicate docstrings.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
