   "sha": "cffeeecd2277469aa947e0580a00b509abfeece4",
   "node_id": "C_kwDOSVPsWtoAKGNmZmVlZWNkMjI3NzQ2OWFhOTQ3ZTA1ODBhMDBiNTA5YWJmZWVjZTQ",
   "commit": {
    "author": {
     "name": "Contributor",
     "email": "dev@example.com",
     "date": "2026-08-24T16:42:47Z"
    },
    "committer": {
     "name": "Contributor",
     "email": "dev@example.com",
     "date": "2026-08-24T16:42:47Z"
    },
    "message": "feat(messaging): surface open messaging auth via startup warnings + admin payload\n\nwhat broke: Telegram/Discord could start with no operator allowlist\n(ALLOWED_TELEGRAM_USER_ID unset / ALLOWED_DISCORD_CHANNELS empty) and\nsilently accept any user or channel as the operator, with no log or\ndashboard signal.\n\nmechanism: component creation in the platform factory is the single site\nthat knows both bot-token and allowlist state; GET /admin/api/config\nalready serializes effective config values for the dashboard.\n\nfix: fire a prominent loguru WARNING once per platform at creation naming\nthe exact risk and its lock variable; add shared predicates\ntelegram_auth_open/discord_auth_open to factory.py and reuse them in\nadmin_routes._messaging_auth_open to expose a top-level\n\"messaging_auth_open\" array ([] when all locked) on the admin config\npayload. Zero runtime behavior change beyond logging + payload.\n\nrun: ruff format && ruff check --fix && ty check; pytest\ntests/messaging/test_messaging_factory.py,\ntests/api/test_admin_messaging_auth_open.py, tests/api/test_admin.py,\ntests/runtime/test_application_runtime.py (+ lifespan, safe-logging,\nfeature-manifest suites) - all passed. All four new guards mutation-checked\nwith failures confirmed by test name; restores byte-equal.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
